# errors.promql — used by tutorial page 3.3 "Errors"
# Scenario: unknown-city.
# Question: did a dependency failure become a user-visible failure?
#
# error.type is a metric attribute stamped only on failed datapoints. The ratio
# is (datapoints carrying error.type) / (all datapoints). The tool ratio reads
# about the Atlantis share; the invocation ratio reads 0, because the tool fails
# but the invocation still succeeds. No native metric can say whether the user
# got weather — that gap is what page 3.7's custom counter fills.
#
# POST each block to:
#   monitoring.googleapis.com/v1/projects/jwd-gcp-demos/location/global/prometheus/api/v1/query
# with body  query=<urlencoded>  and an ADC bearer token.

# --- Tool error ratio ------------------------------------------------------
# Failed tool calls (error.type present) over all tool calls. The demo stamps
# error.type="lookup_failed" via StatusAwareTool on an unknown city.

sum(rate({"gen_ai.execute_tool.duration_count", "error.type"=~".+"}[5m]))
  /
sum(rate({"gen_ai.execute_tool.duration_count"}[5m]))

# Same ratio broken out by tool, so get_weather and get_forecast are separate.

sum by ("gen_ai.tool.name") (
  rate({"gen_ai.execute_tool.duration_count", "error.type"=~".+"}[5m])
)
  /
sum by ("gen_ai.tool.name") (
  rate({"gen_ai.execute_tool.duration_count"}[5m])
)

# --- Invocation error ratio ------------------------------------------------
# Failed invocations over all invocations. Reads 0 for unknown-city: the tool
# failed, the invocation did not.

sum(rate({"gen_ai.invoke_agent.duration_count", "error.type"=~".+"}[5m]))
  /
sum(rate({"gen_ai.invoke_agent.duration_count"}[5m]))
